statement:
Let $n\ge0$, let $L_1,\dots,L_n$ be fields and let $C=L_1\times\cdots\times L_n$ be the product ring (the zero ring for $n=0$), with projections $\pi_j:C\to L_j$. Then:

1. the prime ideals of $C$ are exactly the ideals $\mathfrak p_j=\ker\pi_j=\{(c_1,\dots,c_n):c_j=0\}$, $j=1,\dots,n$, and these are pairwise distinct; so $\operatorname{Spec}C$ [def-weil-affine-spectrum] has exactly $n$ points;
2. the underlying topological space of $\operatorname{Spec}C$ is discrete (every subset is open);
3. for every $j$ the morphism $\operatorname{Spec}\pi_j:\operatorname{Spec}L_j\to\operatorname{Spec}C$ is an open immersion [def-weil-open-immersion] whose image is the one-point set $\{\mathfrak p_j\}$; hence the open subscheme $\{\mathfrak p_j\}$ of $\operatorname{Spec}C$ is isomorphic to $\operatorname{Spec}L_j$ through $\operatorname{Spec}\pi_j$.
